{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeightOneOne_rank_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeightOneOne_rank_one","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L345-L348","doc":"The normalised form of the same statement: `y_{(1,1)} = 0` at `N = 1`, which\nis what the producer returns numerically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalOneOne_rank_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalOneOne_rank_one","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L337-L343","doc":"**The `gl(1)` corner.**  At `N = 1` the antisymmetric specialisation vanishes\nidentically — the cell `(2,1)` has content `−1`, so its numerator factor is\n`[1 + (−1)]_q = [0]_q = 0`.  This is the `n = 2` shadow of\n`OcneanuRankFamily.rowCapFactor_eq_zero`: a partition with more rows than the\nrank dies at the cap cell.  No hypothesis on `q` is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeight_rank_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeight_rank_three","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L327-L333","doc":"**The rank-3 specification from the weights.**  `z_3 = q⁵/(q⁴+q²+1)`, what a\nflavour `SU(3)` trace on the same `H_n(q)` would have to carry.  A specification,\nnot a construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeight_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeight_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L319-L325","doc":"**Convention D from the weights.**  At `N = 2` the hook-content weights give\n`z = q³/(q²+1)` — the corpus's canonical Markov parameter (owner ruling\n2026-08-15 R1).  So convention D is not a normalisation choice: it is the `SU(2)`\nprincipal specialisation, cell by cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.hookContent_markovParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.hookContent_markovParam","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L296-L317","doc":"**The hook-content weights give `markovParam`.**\n\n`tr_M(σ) = y_{(2)}·q + y_{(1,1)}·(−q⁻¹) = (q − q⁻¹)q^{2N}/(q^{2N} − 1)`, for\nevery rank `N ≥ 1` and every `q > 1`, with the left side built from the\nhook-content product over the four named cells of the two partitions of `2` and\nthe right side taken unchanged from `OcneanuRankFamily`.\n\nThis is the `n = 2` instance of the hook-content principal-specialisation\nidentity that `OcneanuRankFamily`'s module docstring cites rather than proves.\nIt is **not** the general formula — see this file's docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schur_combo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schur_combo","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L275-L292","doc":"**The unnormalised trace is `[N]_q · q^N`** — `s_{(2)}·q + s_{(1,1)}·(−q⁻¹)`,\nby `q[N+1]_q − q⁻¹[N−1]_q = q^N[2]_q`.  The two coefficients are the eigenvalues\nof `σ` on the two blocks of `H_2(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schur_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schur_sum","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L260-L273","doc":"**The Markov normaliser is `[N]_q²`** — `s_{(2)} + s_{(1,1)} = [N]_q²`, by\n`[N+1]_q + [N−1]_q = [2]_q[N]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalOneOne_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalOneOne_eq","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L252-L258","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalTwo_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalTwo_eq","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L244-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeightOneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeightOneOne","kind":"def","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L240-L242","doc":"`y_{(1,1)}`, normalised by the same Markov condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeightTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.markovWeightTwo","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L235-L238","doc":"`y_{(2)}`, normalised by the Markov condition `Σ_λ y_λ f^λ = 1`.  At `n = 2`\nboth `f^λ = 1`, so the normaliser is the bare sum of the two specialisations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalOneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalOneOne","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L228-L233","doc":"`s_{(1,1)}(1, q, …, q^{N-1})` up to a `q`-power, written as the hook-content\nproduct over the two cells of `(1,1)`: `(1,1)` with content `0` and hook `2`,\nand `(2,1)` with content `−1` and hook `1`.  The `−1` is the cell that carries\nthe row cap: at `N = 1` it makes the index `0` and the whole weight vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.schurPrincipalTwo","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L222-L226","doc":"`s_{(2)}(1, q, …, q^{N-1})` up to a `q`-power, written as the hook-content\nproduct over the two cells of `(2)`: `(1,1)` with content `0` and hook `2`, and\n`(1,2)` with content `1` and hook `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.cellFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.cellFactor","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L217-L220","doc":"The hook-content factor of a single cell of content `c` and hook length `h`\nin a rank-`N` principal specialisation: `[N + c]_q / [h]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_mul_markovParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_mul_markovParam","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L200-L213","doc":"**`[N]_q · markovParam N q = q^N`**, i.e. the closed form of\n`OcneanuRankFamily` is `q^N/[N]_q`.  This is the one-line content of the whole\nhook-content identity at `n = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_pos","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L191-L198","doc":"`[N]_q > 0` for `N ≥ 1` and `q > 1` — what lets the normalisation be\ndivided by. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_two_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_two_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L186-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.hecke_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.hecke_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L183-L184","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_shift_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_shift_diff","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L169-L179","doc":"**`q·[m+1]_q − q⁻¹·[m−1]_q = q^m · [2]_q`.**  The identity that produces the\nnumerator `tr_M(σ)`: the eigenvalues `q` on the symmetric block and `−q⁻¹` on\nthe antisymmetric one enter exactly here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_shift_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_shift_sum","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L157-L167","doc":"**`[m+1]_q + [m−1]_q = [2]_q · [m]_q`.**  The identity that collapses the\nMarkov normalisation `s_{(2)} + s_{(1,1)}` to `[N]_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L153-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L149-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_two","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L140-L147","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`.  The hook-`2` cell of both `n = 2` partitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_one","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L136-L138","doc":"`[1]_q = 1`.  This is why the hook-`1` cells contribute no denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.sq_sub_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.sq_sub_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L128-L134","doc":"`q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0` forces `q² − 1 ≠ 0`, since `q − q⁻¹ = (q² − 1)/q`.  Needed\nbecause `field_simp` clears `q⁻¹` and then meets `q² − 1` in the denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HookContentMarkovParam.qIntBalanced_eq","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HookContentMarkovParam.lean#L122-L126","doc":"`qIntBalanced` with the negative exponent written as an inverse — the form\nevery algebraic step below runs on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}